The probes confirmed that a payload containing terminal escape sequences can pass `MATCH` and still assemble with a valid signature. They also confirmed that `assemble` reports a replacement software key as “the repository root.” The normal build passed the payload round-trip and armor checks. I’ll document these findings alongside the missing SHA-1DC check and the procedure’s limits on authenticating NUC-supplied fingerprints.
